From 314f1963db3e507f5e149b5d305703a713677bae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yeison Delgado <yeisonestivendelgado109@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:05:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(device): inactive devices with their inactivity alarms
 (US17, F-38 to F-40, NF-08)

GET /device/inactive?hours=24 lists the devices of the user scope that
were inactive in the window, with their inactivity periods. A period is
the device's inactivity alarm: it opens at its previous record plus its
threshold (F-38) and resolves by itself at its next stored record (F-39);
end is null while it is open. Devices inactive now come first, oldest
last record first (F-40), then the ones that reported again. Each device
also carries its energy level and low_energy against the new settings
FALCON_LOW_ENERGY_PERCENT and SMAC_LOW_ENERGY_PERCENT (30 % by default,
NF-08 and client answer CL-11).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
